          "Psychologists studying the Overview Effect note that experiencing this 'self-transcendent awe' shrinks the human ego and expands our circle of empathy from our local tribe or nation to the entire biosphere. As astronomer Carl Sagan famously wrote when the Voyager 1 spacecraft took a final photograph of Earth from six billion kilometres away — where our planet appeared as a 'Pale Blue Dot' suspended in a sunbeam — it underscores our duty to deal more kindly with one another, and to preserve and cherish the only home we have ever known.",
