        "How did 'Gödel numbering' allow a mathematical formula about numbers to talk about itself?|By assigning a unique prime-number code to every mathematical symbol, formula, and proof|By writing equations in invisible ink|By using Roman numerals instead of Arabic numerals|By translating numbers into musical notes",
        "In Gödel's proof, why can't a consistent mathematical system prove statement G ('Statement G cannot be proved')?|Because if the system proved G, then G would be false, meaning the system proves false statements (making it inconsistent)|Because statement G is too long to write on paper|Because prime numbers cannot be multiplied|Because the system has no symbols for addition",
        "Since statement G cannot be proved within a consistent system, what must be true about G?|Statement G is true (because it truly cannot be proved), yet it remains unprovable within the system|Statement G is completely false and meaningless|Statement G is equal to zero|Statement G disappears from arithmetic",
