          "When a robot clearly looks like a mechanical toy or a friendly cartoon character — with round metal eyes and simple limbs — we find it charming because our brain categorizes it as a machine and delights in its human-like gestures. However, when designers give a robot synthetic silicone skin, glass eyes, and realistic hair so that it looks ninety-five percent human, our emotional response suddenly plunges into a deep trough of revulsion, eeriness, and unease! Only when the likeness reaches 100% — indistinguishable from a living person — does affinity climb back up out of this 'Uncanny Valley'.",
